## Source model

The DCM source model was defined as a six-source auditory hierarchy based on the Phillips et al. frequency-deviant model architecture. The source order was fixed because this order determines the interpretation of all A, B, and C matrices.

| Source number | Source name | MNI X | MNI Y | MNI Z |
|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|
| 1 | left A1 | -42 | -22 | 7 |
| 2 | right A1 | 46 | -14 | 8 |
| 3 | left STG | -61 | -32 | 8 |
| 4 | right STG | 59 | -25 | 8 |
| 5 | left IFG | -46 | 20 | 8 |
| 6 | right IFG | 46 | 20 | 8 |

The right-hemisphere coordinates were aligned with the Phillips source set, and the left IFG coordinate was implemented as the mirrored homologue of the right IFG coordinate.

---

## Model architecture

The model was implemented as a working version of the Phillips et al. frequency-deviant winning architecture, model 12.

The model includes:

- sensory driving input to bilateral A1;
- bidirectional A1-STG connections within each hemisphere;
- bidirectional STG-IFG connections within each hemisphere;
- lateral IFG-to-IFG connectivity;
- Pitch Deviant modulation of included extrinsic connections;
- intrinsic modulation of bilateral A1 in the B matrix;
- no IFG expectancy input.

The absence of IFG expectancy input is important because the current model targets the pitch/frequency deviant, not the duration/gap temporal-structure deviants.

